<!--
  Inner body for the "Interactive Input — alert user on run page" optional job property, shown when the
  operator ticks the enable checkbox in Configure. The toggle has no further fields; this only explains
  what enabling it does.
-->
<j:jelly xmlns:j="jelly:core" xmlns:f="/lib/form">
  <f:description>
    When enabled, each build's page shows a summary row that stays hidden until this build is waiting
    for interactive input, then reveals with an "input needed" cue (the same live behaviour as the
    inline box on the job page). It only affects what the run page displays — it never changes how the
    build runs.
  </f:description>
</j:jelly>
